# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
.claude
/data
dist
.env
.env.*
src-tauri/target
dist-ssr
*.local

# ─── Belt-and-suspenders: never commit runtime / user data ──────────────────
# /data (above) already covers the dev data directory where these normally
# live. These extra patterns catch a sensitive file even if a stray copy ever
# ended up somewhere else in the tree (e.g. dragged to the repo root to inspect
# it). The .enc envelopes and the lock hash are the crown jewels; losing those
# to a public commit is the one outcome worth being paranoid about.
*.enc
lock.json
budget-*.json
time-tracker.json
draft.json
settings.json
*-settings.json
custom-themes.json
shell-state.json
window.json
auto-backup.json
auto-backup-presets.json
backups/

# Atomic-write temp files (pid-tagged) and tool outputs, in case any were ever
# produced inside the repo during testing.
*.tmp-*
robocopy_log_*.txt
files-generated-*/
resized-*/

# Build-generated copies in public/ (created by copy-public-docs.mjs:
# the originals at the repo root are the tracked source of truth)
public/README.md
public/LICENSE
public/LICENSING.md
public/ATTRIBUTION.md
public/CHANGELOG.json
public/CONTRIBUTING.md
public/SECURITY.md
public/swiss-rb-knife-logo.png
public/screenshots/

# Sound attribution notes. The credit lines from each sound's source, kept
# next to the audio while a pack is being put together and consolidated by
# hand into ATTRIBUTION.md, which is the tracked source of truth. Untracked
# because they are working notes, not a deliverable; the licenses they record
# live in ATTRIBUTION.md, and scripts/checks/settings.test.mjs fails if a
# shipped sound has no entry there.
attr/

# Tauri-generated schemas (regenerated on every dev/build)
src-tauri/gen/schemas

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Windows junk
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
# Whole-folder import staging, and the folders an import sets aside. Both are
# named after the data folder and sit beside it (see
# src-tauri/src/data_archive.rs), so in a dev build they land at the repo root
# next to /data.
/data.srbk-incoming
/data.srbk-replaced-*

# Local working notes (see dev/ for the checklist and standards docs)
/dev
# Temporary storage for supporting files that help guide development goals
/demo

# Built by scripts/build-agent.mjs for Tauri's externalBin. A build artifact of
# the src-tauri/agent crate, not a checked-in binary.
/src-tauri/binaries
